      "provenance": {
        "notes": "The 01e baseline expected severity 1 (sharp needles, pets avoid it); both fetched toxicity sources (ASPCA and NC State's non-toxic tags for cats and dogs) say non-toxic, so 0. NC State notes the leaf tips are sharp-pointed. Light: Iowa State 'bright light' near an east, west or south window, NC State bright with some afternoon shade; mapped to bright_indirect. Temperature: Iowa State 55 to 70 F, NC State 55 to 65 F. Growth rate: NC State says rapid, which fits the tree outdoors; RHS implies slow (over 50 years to maturity) and indoor plants are said to reach about 9 ft; treat as unreliable. Size: houseplants stay near 9 ft (NC State) but no spread is given, so unknown. Humidity: Iowa State says winter air is too dry, no number."
      },
